I wanted to do a speed run. I admittedly did startscum for a magic
marker, but other starting equipment was unremarkable. Thankfully, the
shop's equipment *was* remarkable: a pair of +1 speed boots in an
armor dealership, a magic lamp (traded for +2 SDSM), *second* magic
marker, and bag of holding at minetown, and a coaligned altar on level
4. Oh, and a spellbook of identify in a scroll shop too.

Even with all that equipment, my hazardous early-game playing style of
diving headlong into the Gnomish mines nearly killed me on several
occasions. I knew that I'd need daggers early on, so I assembled a
stack of 17 +0 daggers on my way down to the luckstone. Once I
increased my luck, I wrote a spellbook of create monster, and scrolls
of enchant armor and charging. My AC was -16, even without divine
protection. Furthermore, I somehow managed to find rings of
teleportation and teleport control.

After enchanting the daggers to +7 and getting to "skilled" in dagger,
along with obtaining Magicbane, I descended at a furious pace. I only
briefly stopped on the level above medusa, when I found a huge throne
room near a chaotic altar. I used a scroll of earth to create a
"funnel" for monsters near the altar, shouted some insults at the
royalty, and sacrificed several monsters. When I got a cockatrice
corpse (and a wand of digging from some poor royal shmuck), I decided
it was time to storm the castle. I created another "rock fort" in
front of the castle, plunked down a scroll of scare monster, and
crashed down the drawbridge at turn 8000. The castle occupants didn't
know what hit them. I took a (0:3) wand of wishing with little
resistance, thanks to Magicbane and magic missile.

On the way back up to the quest, I found Knight bones with Excalibur
and Sunsword, along with a wand of wishing and plenty of blank
scrolls. I wished for a wand of polymorph and got rings of free
action, levitation, and conflict, along with a charged-up +5 ring of
increase damage. I lost way too much time here - the nurse dancing,
polypiling, and stash-sorting took around 3500 turns, almost as many
as Gehennom itself! Sadly, polypiling doesn't pay unless you have a
lot of junk. In a faster speed run, I doubt any of my material would
have been junk. The biggest payoff was really polypiling spellbooks,
which netted fireball, cone of cold, light, remove curse, and several
other toys.

Gehennom passed without incident; when you can cast magic mapping,
detect treasure, and dig on a regular basis, hell freezes over. The
demon lords were pushovers, summoning swarms fell to conflict without
fail. Massed foes fell to magic missile, while minotaurs and Arch-
lichs were decimated by my effectively +11 daggers. I never missed the
extra ring slot.

The ascension run was worrysome since I had no means to confuse myself
- no forgotten spells! Thankfully I had several cursed blank scrolls,
so cursed confused monster and gold detection scrolls bailed me out
for portal detection. Also, I never got crowned or learned Finger of
Death, so Rodney fell to Orcus's wand.

At one point air elementals reduced me to 35 HP, so I started using up
wands of death and polymorph like mad. Then I realized they weren't
sleep resistant. Sure enough, two or three spells rendered the living
tornados inert, allowing me to destroy them with magic missile.
Unfortunately, I had no death zaps or poly zaps left after my initial
panic and only realized in the middle of Astral. Thankfully, I wished
for a cockatrice corpse ( the (0:3) wand was still (0:2)!) and cleared
a path to the first - and correct - altar.

I can definitely see room for improvement, since all I *really* needed
to pwn the castle was reflection and a footrice corpse, and all I
needed to *reach* the castle was a ring of teleport control or a bunch
of wands of digging, both of which are not significantly difficult to
obtain. I don't think I'll be beating Eidolos anytime soon, but I'm
still pround of my first sub-20K (actually first sub 60K!) ascension.
And I'm heartily reminded of how much easier nethack wizards are than
sporkhack's.




